// listNodePortAllocations implements BACKLOG.md "still open" #11: `AM1` is a
// `NodePort` conflict between two Services, confidence 1.00, correct
// escalation — and no plan, because the catalogue's scalar alternative
// ("give one Service a different nodePort") was, in the model's own words,
// an unverifiable guess: nothing let it check what was already allocated
// cluster-wide, so proposing a specific replacement might just relocate the
// conflict onto a third Service instead of resolving it. This tool answers
// exactly that question, targeted (is port X already taken, and by what) or
// surveyed (what's allocated in a bounded window), so the investigation loop
// can verify a candidate before proposing it rather than guessing.
//
// NodePort allocation is inherently cluster-wide — a nodePort in namespace A
// collides with one in namespace B; the API server tracks one shared
// per-protocol allocation table, not one per namespace — so unlike this
// file's other list_* tool (list_resources), there is no narrower namespace
// to scope this to. That is a deliberate, stated exception to this
// codebase's usual single-namespace-scoping discipline, not an oversight:
// the question this tool answers literally cannot be asked within one
